# Config Examples

## Diff Tool Config

```xml
<config>
	<values>
		<VALUE_MINIMUM_LONGEST_COMMON_SUBSTRING>12</VALUE_MINIMUM_LONGEST_COMMON_SUBSTRING>
		<COUNTER_FULL_REVISION>1000</COUNTER_FULL_REVISION>
	</values>
	<externals>
		<sevenzip>"D:\Programme\Utilities\7-Zip\7z.exe"</sevenzip>
	</externals>
	<input>
		<MODE_SURROGATES>DISCARD_REVISION</MODE_SURROGATES>
		<WIKIPEDIA_ENCODING>UTF-8</WIKIPEDIA_ENCODING>
		<archive>
			<type>SEVENZIP</type>
			<path>"D:\simplewiki.7z"</path>
			<start>0</start>
		</archive>
	</input>
	<output>
		<OUTPUT_MODE>SQL</OUTPUT_MODE>
		<PATH>""</PATH>
		<LIMIT_SQL_FILE_SIZE>1000000000</LIMIT_SQL_FILE_SIZE>
		<MODE_ZIP_COMPRESSION_ENABLED>true</MODE_ZIP_COMPRESSION_ENABLED>
	</output>
	<cache>
		<LIMIT_TASK_SIZE_REVISIONS>5000000</LIMIT_TASK_SIZE_REVISIONS>
		<LIMIT_TASK_SIZE_DIFFS>1000000</LIMIT_TASK_SIZE_DIFFS>
		<LIMIT_SQLSERVER_MAX_ALLOWED_PACKET>1000000</LIMIT_SQLSERVER_MAX_ALLOWED_PACKET>
	</cache>
	<logging>
		<root_folder>""</root_folder>
		<diff_tool>
			<level>INFO</level>
		</diff_tool>
	</logging>
	<debug>
		<verification_diff>false</verification_diff>
		<verification_encoding>false</verification_encoding>
		<statistical_output>false</statistical_output>
		<debug_output>
			<enabled>false</enabled>
			<path>""</path>
		</debug_output>
	</debug>
	<filter>
		<namespaces>
			<!-- White list of namespaces; if nothing here then all namespaces are allowed -->
			<ns>0</ns>
			<ns>1</ns>
		</namespaces>
	</filter>
</config>

```

## Index Generator Config

```
host=localhost
db=wiki_en_20110405_rev
user=student
password=student
output=target
outputDatabase=false
outputDatafile=false
charset=UTF8
buffer=15000
maxAllowedPackets=16760832
```

## Indexes on the revisions table

The DiffTool declares `articleIdx (ArticleID, RevisionCounter)` when it creates
the `revisions` table and builds it once after the bulk load. After the index
tables have been generated, the index generator enables the keys of the
`revisions` table and creates the following secondary indexes if they are
missing:

```sql
CREATE INDEX articleIdx ON revisions(ArticleID, RevisionCounter);
CREATE INDEX articleTsIdx ON revisions(ArticleID, Timestamp, RevisionCounter);
```

The composite index `articleTsIdx` allows timestamp-based lookups of an article
(e.g. `getRevisionTimestamps(...)` or `getRevision(articleID, Timestamp)`) to be
answered from the index instead of reading every revision row of the article.

Revision databases created with an earlier version can be migrated with the
following statement (on large MyISAM tables this rebuilds the index file and
may take several hours):

```sql
ALTER TABLE revisions ADD INDEX articleTsIdx (ArticleID, Timestamp, RevisionCounter);
```
